{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits"]]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"anatomy-of-a-game.png","type":"image"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". That one type carries everything: the rooms and things, where they start, and the rules that govern them. This article is the model underneath — how the engine finds your declarations, how one value is both a declaration and a live reference, and how the world that never changes is kept apart from the state that does.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Declarations-are-stored-properties","text":"Declarations are stored properties","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rooms, things, and custom state are declared as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stored properties"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" of the game type:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\") }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When you construct the world with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld\/init(game:saveDirectory:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the engine’s bootstrap reflects over the game value with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mirror","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and collects every ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It names each entity after the property it was stored in: ","type":"text"},{"code":"foyer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" becomes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"foyer\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"cloak","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" becomes ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"cloak\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and so on. You never write these IDs by hand — the property name ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the name.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is why declarations must live in the type’s main body, not an extension: Swift only allows stored properties there, and the Mirror only sees stored properties. (When even the declarations need to span files or ship separately, that is what a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" bundle is for — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".)","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"One-value-two-roles","text":"One value, two roles","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A declaration and a live reference are the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same value"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }   \/\/ the declaration","","\/\/ …later, inside a rule body:","cloak.after(.take) {","    if cloak.isWorn { … }        \/\/ the live reference — reads current state","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"cloak","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value. Written in the game body it ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declares"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the cloak. Used in a rule it ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reads and writes the live cloak’s state"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and so on all consult the current turn.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This works because each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" mints a private identity token when it is created. The token — not the struct’s contents — is the entity’s identity, and it survives copying. Two items are equal when they share a token (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Inside a turn, the token resolves to the entity’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and then to its state; outside a turn there is no state to read, so a live property access traps with an explanation rather than returning a meaningless value.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"References are always compile-checked. ","type":"text"},{"code":"cloak.after(.take)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"hook.holds(cloak)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"foyer.north(bar)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — every one is ordinary property access, so renaming a room or deleting an item breaks the build instead of the running game.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Scenery","text":"Scenery","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every noun a room description names should answer when the player examines it. Declare a fixture with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/scenery(_:adjectives:synonyms:description:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let wall = Item.scenery(","    \"stone wall\", adjectives: \"rough\", synonyms: \"masonry\", \"old brickwork\",","    description: \"Mortar fills the cracks.\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This creates an ordinary ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with a name, vocabulary, examine text, and the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/scenery","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" trait. The fixture cannot be taken and gets no stock room-listing sentence. The name and synonyms contribute nouns and adjectives through the usual parser rules: ","type":"text"},{"code":"stone wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" answers to ","type":"text"},{"code":"wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"stone wall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"old brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the adjective ","type":"text"},{"code":"old","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"adjectives:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"synonyms:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are variadic, so they read the way "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/synonyms(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" read inside an "},{"code":"Item { }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block — one phrase per argument, no brackets. A synonym is a noun phrase, not a single word, which is why "},{"code":"old brickwork","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" above counts as one argument."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A phrase that ends in one of the item’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"nouns","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a name, and names are matched first. A phrase that doesn’t — "},{"code":"x rough","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"take velvet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — is a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"description","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and the parser answers one when it picks out exactly one thing in view and asks "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"“Which do you mean…?”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when it picks out several. Second pass, always: a description can never take a phrase away from something that already answered to it as a name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Store it on your game or content bundle and place it in "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", just like any other item:"}]},{"code":["var map: WorldMap {","    player.starts(in: hall)","    wall.starts(in: hall)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All arguments after the name are optional. Use the trailing trait block when scenery has another role:"}]},{"code":["let niche = Item.scenery(\"shadowed niche\", synonyms: \"alcove\") {","    container","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The niche can hold things and take item rules. For text that turns on the niche’s own state — open or shut, lit or dark — omit "},{"code":"description:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and put "},{"code":"description(when: \\.isOpen, …, otherwise: …)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the trait block; for text that depends on anything else, attach a "},{"code":"niche.describe { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rule. Without any description, examining it uses the game’s stock examine line. Placement determines where a piece of scenery is visible, just as it does for other items."}]},{"anchor":"The-parts-of-the-Game-protocol","text":"The parts of the `Game` protocol","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" gathers a handful of members, most with defaults so a small game declares only what it needs:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"intro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tagline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the banner and scoring metadata.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — geography and initial placement, as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap"},{"text":". Read once at startup to build the initial state.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — all game logic, as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules"},{"text":" value. Defaults to empty.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — player-typeable verbs this game adds, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[SyntaxRule]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Defaults to empty. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — content bundles the game composes itself from, as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents"},{"text":". Defaults to empty. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"noiseWords","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — filler words the parser drops from input before matching, beside the built-in articles, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"[String]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A spell game adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"spell\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so ","type":"text"},{"code":"cast the glow spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parses as ","type":"text"},{"code":"cast glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Defaults to empty; a noise word that is also a verb, preposition, direction, item word, or one of the words the parser claims for itself — the pronouns, the multi-object keywords, the conjunction, the exception words, the possessives — is a fatal diagnostic, since stripping it would make the word untypeable.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The protocol extension also hands every game three ambient references usable as bare identifiers inside "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player"},{"text":", for its location, score, and inventory, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item"},{"text":" for the player as a thing in the world (what ","type":"text"},{"code":"X ME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" examines).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World"},{"text":", for rules that apply everywhere (like daemons).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command"},{"text":" currently being performed, inside a rule body.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"The-map-block","text":"The `map` block","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a result-builder property that yields a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — a flat list of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" statements: exits, initial item placements, and the player’s start."}]},{"code":["var map: WorldMap {","    foyer.south(bar)                 \/\/ an exit","    bar.north(foyer)                 \/\/ and the way back, stated separately","","    player.starts(in: foyer)         \/\/ where the player begins","    cloak.startsWorn                 \/\/ where each thing begins","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-way, so an asymmetric map needs no special case. There are five kinds of exit and eight ways to place a thing; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMapAndExits","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" covers all of them."}]},{"anchor":"Immutable-definition-mutable-state","text":"Immutable definition, mutable state","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Internally, the engine keeps two things strictly apart:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"definition","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is everything that never changes during play: names, descriptions, exits, rules, and the parser’s vocabulary. It is built once, from your declarations, at startup.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is everything that ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does","type":"text"}]},{"text":" change: where each item is, what is lit, the score, the turn count, which things have been touched, and your ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global"},{"text":" values.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The entire mutable state is a single "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Every change funnels through it, so a turn commits atomically at its end (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and save\/restore is a serialization call rather than a feature threaded through the codebase."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you write "},{"code":"cloak.isWorn","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"player.score += 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule, you are reading and writing that one state value through the entity’s token — never touching the definition, and never seeing another turn’s half-finished changes."}]},{"anchor":"See-also","text":"See also","type":"heading","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"Anatomy of a Game"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Rules":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The collected rules of a game, declared in one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"text":" block. Large games","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compose: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var rules: Rules { cloakRules; barRules }"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Rules","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/rules","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Location","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","type":"topic","title":"Location","abstract":[{"text":"A place in the world.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Location","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"title":"Gnusto","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","role":"collection"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameContents":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamecontents","title":"GameContents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameContents"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The collected content bundles a game declares, in declaration order.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameContents"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GettingStarted":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Command":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Command","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A parsed player command, available inside rule bodies as ","type":"text"},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Command","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/command","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Command","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/name":{"abstract":[{"text":"The item’s display name.","type":"text"}],"title":"name","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/name","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Player":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Player","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The player character, available as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVo